Description: Boswas OS desktop: compositor, shell and session
 The native Boswas OS desktop, written in Rust. It takes the place of KWin,
 the Plasma shell and the Plasma session; applications keep working because
 it speaks the standard Wayland protocols.
 .
  * boswas-compositor: the Wayland compositor (on the Smithay library): the
    display server, window manager and effects engine. Floating windows with
    Boswas frames, snap layouts, workspaces, Alt+Tab, fractional scaling;
    DRM/KMS with OpenGL ES on real hardware, a software renderer for tests
  * boswas-shell: wallpaper, panel and launcher, the lock screen and the
    login screen
  * boswas-session: the session greetd starts after login
 .
 Security model: ordinary applications cannot read the screen, other
 windows or global key strokes. Panels, the lock screen, the window list and
 clipboard control are offered only to the programs the compositor starts
 itself; sandboxed applications never see them. The compositor owns the
 session lock: a locked screen stays blank even if the lock screen crashes.
 The session locks after ten minutes without input, and a user cannot
 lengthen that.
 .
 greetd is pointed at /etc/boswas/greetd.toml by a systemd drop-in; its own
 configuration file is not modified.
